IMPORT prelude

-- Trade Disputes Act 1941 (Singapore) -- what counts as industrial action, when a strike or lockout is illegal (ss 2, 3, 4), the
-- offences and their maximum penalties (ss 5 to 11), protection for those who refuse to join an illegal strike (s 8), picketing
-- (s 10), the procedural rules for prosecution (ss 12 to 14) and the conspiracy shield (s 15).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 15/9/2026"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TDA1941.txt. The cover says it incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the text annotates
-- later amendments by Act 30 of 2021 (wef 2 November 2022), Act 30 of 2024 (the Platform Workers Act changes, wef 1 January 2025)
-- and Act 10 of 2025 (s 15(4A), wef 15 September 2026).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it decides when an employee, or since 2025 a platform worker such as a
-- delivery rider or private-hire driver, may lawfully strike, picket or refuse to strike, and what happens if they do. SCOPED to
-- nearly the whole operative Act (it has 15 sections). Not encoded: s 1 (short title), the definitions of "award", "injury" and
-- "platform operator" beyond their effect, the Platform Workers Act 2024 definitions that s 2 borrows (not read), and the
-- Industrial Relations Act 1960 machinery that decides when an Industrial Arbitration Court "has cognizance".
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Trade Disputes Act 1941 -- industrial action`

§§ `2 -- industrial action, strike, trade dispute, work dispute`

-- s 2 "industrial action": (a) "any act or omission by a body of persons employed in any trade or industry, acting in combination
-- or under a common understanding, which would result in any limitation or restriction on, or delay in, the performance of any
-- duties connected with their employment"; (b) the same for a body of persons providing a platform service; or (c) a strike.
-- "strike": "the cessation of work" by such a body acting in combination, "or a concerted refusal, or a refusal under a common
-- understanding ... to continue to work or to accept employment" (or, for platform workers, to accept tasks).
-- So a go-slow or work-to-rule is industrial action, not only a walk-out; a lone worker is not "a body of persons".
GIVEN `employees or platform workers` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acting in combination or under a common understanding` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `stopping or refusing work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `limiting, restricting or delaying their duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is industrial action` IF
        `employees or platform workers`
    AND `acting in combination or under a common understanding`
    AND (`stopping or refusing work` OR `limiting, restricting or delaying their duties`)

-- "trade dispute": any dispute "between employers and employees or between employees and employees, or between employers and
-- employers which is connected with the employment or non-employment, or the terms of employment or the conditions of labour, of
-- any person". "work dispute": between platform workers and platform operators, between platform workers, or between platform
-- operators, connected with whether a person is engaged as a platform worker or the terms or conditions of the service.
DECLARE Parties IS ONE OF
    `employers and employees`
    `employees and employees`
    `employers and employers`
    `platform operators and platform workers`
    `platform workers and platform workers`
    `platform operators and platform operators`
    `a union and the Government`

GIVEN `the parties` IS A Parties, `connected with employment or its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a trade dispute or work dispute` IF
        `connected with employment or its terms`
    AND CONSIDER `the parties`
        WHEN `a union and the Government` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 and 4 -- illegal industrial action and illegal lockout`

-- s 3(1): an industrial action "shall be illegal if" (a) "it has any object other than the furtherance of" a trade dispute within
-- the trade or industry in which the participants are engaged, or a work dispute about the platform service they provide; (b) "it
-- is in furtherance of a trade dispute or work dispute of which an Industrial Arbitration Court has cognizance"; or (c) "it is
-- designed or calculated to coerce the Government either directly or by inflicting hardship on the community".
-- s 3(2): the same three tests for a lockout, by reference to the employers' (or platform operators') own trade or service.
-- s 4: "A lockout in consequence of an illegal industrial action or an industrial action in consequence of an illegal lockout shall
-- not be deemed to be illegal."
-- "any object other than": a sympathy strike for workers in another industry, or a political strike, fails (a) even if it ALSO
-- furthers a genuine dispute.
GIVEN `has any object beyond its own trade's or service's dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an Industrial Arbitration Court has cognizance of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `designed to coerce the Government` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in consequence of an illegal lockout` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the industrial action is illegal` IF
        (NOT `in consequence of an illegal lockout`)
    AND (   `has any object beyond its own trade's or service's dispute`
         OR `an Industrial Arbitration Court has cognizance of the dispute`
         OR `designed to coerce the Government`)

GIVEN `has any object beyond its own trade's or service's dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an Industrial Arbitration Court has cognizance of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `designed to coerce the Government` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in consequence of an illegal industrial action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lockout is illegal` IF
        (NOT `in consequence of an illegal industrial action`)
    AND (   `has any object beyond its own trade's or service's dispute`
         OR `an Industrial Arbitration Court has cognizance of the dispute`
         OR `designed to coerce the Government`)

§§ `5 to 11 -- offences and maximum penalties`

-- s 5(1): commencing, continuing or acting in furtherance of an illegal industrial action -- fine up to $2,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 5(2): the same for an illegal lockout -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 6: instigating or inciting others to take part in an illegal industrial action or lockout, "or who instigates or incites a
-- person bound by an award to take part in ... ANY industrial action" -- $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 7: "knowingly expends or applies any money in direct furtherance or support of any illegal industrial action or lockout" --
-- $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 8(2): a registered trade union or registered platform work association that penalises a refuser -- fine up to $5,000 (no
-- imprisonment).
-- s 9: intimidation -- $2,000 or 3 months or both. s 10: unlawful picketing "shall be deemed to constitute an offence under
-- section 9(d)". s 11: dangerous breach of contract -- $2,000 or 3 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `taking part in an illegal industrial action`
    `taking part in an illegal lockout`
    `instigating an illegal industrial action or lockout`
    `inciting a person bound by an award to industrial action`
    `funding an illegal industrial action or lockout`
    `a union penalising a member who refused`
    `intimidation`
    `unlawful picketing`
    `dangerous breach of contract`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal industrial action` THEN 2000
    WHEN `intimidation` THEN 2000
    WHEN `unlawful picketing` THEN 2000
    WHEN `dangerous breach of contract` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal industrial action` THEN 6
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal lockout` THEN 6
    WHEN `instigating an illegal industrial action or lockout` THEN 12
    WHEN `inciting a person bound by an award to industrial action` THEN 12
    WHEN `funding an illegal industrial action or lockout` THEN 12
    WHEN `a union penalising a member who refused` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 3

-- s 6, second limb: inciting a person bound by an award is an offence whatever the legality of the action.
GIVEN `incited others to take part` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the action is illegal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person incited is bound by an award` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incitement is an offence` IF
    `incited others to take part` AND (`the action is illegal` OR `the person incited is bound by an award`)

GIVEN `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN, `in direct furtherance or support` IS A BOOLEAN, `the action is illegal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `spending the money is an offence` IF
    `knowingly` AND `in direct furtherance or support` AND `the action is illegal`

§§ `8 -- refusing to take part`

-- s 8(1): "No person who refuses to take part in or to continue to take part in an illegal industrial action or lockout shall, by
-- reason of such refusal, be subject to expulsion from any trade union or platform work association or to any fine or penalty, or
-- to any deprivation of any right or benefit ... nor ... at any disadvantage as compared with other members".
-- s 8(2): if "a registered trade union or registered platform work association" (or its managing body) "declares that it expels or
-- intends to expel" or penalises a member contrary to (1), the union is guilty of an offence.
-- The protection is for refusing an ILLEGAL action; the Act says nothing about refusing a lawful one.
GIVEN `the action refused was illegal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the penalty is by reason of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refuser is protected` IF
    `the action refused was illegal` AND `the penalty is by reason of the refusal`

GIVEN `the union is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `declared an expulsion or penalty, or an intention to impose one` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the action refused was illegal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the penalty is by reason of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the union commits the s 8(2) offence` IF
        `the union is registered`
    AND `declared an expulsion or penalty, or an intention to impose one`
    AND `the refuser is protected` `the action refused was illegal` `the penalty is by reason of the refusal`

§§ `9 -- intimidation`

-- s 9: every person who "with a view to compelling any other person to abstain from doing or to do any act, which such other person
-- has a legal right to do or abstain from doing, wrongfully and without legal authority" (a) "uses violence to or intimidates such
-- other person or his wife or children, or injures his property"; (b) "persistently follows such other person about from place to
-- place"; (c) hides his tools, clothes or other property or hinders him in their use; (d) "watches or besets the house or other
-- place where such other person resides or works or carries on business or happens to be"; or (e) "follows such other person with 2
-- or more persons in a disorderly manner in or through any street or road".
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `using violence on him`
    `intimidating his wife or children`
    `injuring his property`
    `persistently following him`
    `following him once`
    `hiding his tools`
    `besetting his home`
    `following him with 2 or more others in a disorderly manner`
    `following him with 2 or more others in an orderly manner`
    `arguing with him`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a listed means` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `following him once` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `following him with 2 or more others in an orderly manner` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `arguing with him` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct,
      `to compel him to do or not do what he has a legal right to do or not do` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wrongfully and without legal authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is intimidation under s 9` IF
        `the conduct is a listed means` `the conduct`
    AND `to compel him to do or not do what he has a legal right to do or not do`
    AND `wrongfully and without legal authority`

§§ `10 -- picketing`

-- s 10: "It shall not be unlawful" for persons acting on their own behalf or for a trade union, employer, platform work association
-- or platform operator "in contemplation or furtherance of a trade dispute" (or work dispute) "to attend at or near a house or place
-- where a person resides or works ... (a) merely for the purpose of peacefully obtaining or communicating information; or (b) merely
-- for the purpose of peacefully persuading or inducing any person to work or abstain from working, except that if such person or
-- persons so attends ... in such numbers or otherwise in such manner as to be calculated -- (c) to intimidate any person ...; (d) to
-- obstruct the approach to or exit from that house or place; or (e) to lead to a breach of the peace, such attending shall be
-- unlawful and shall be deemed to constitute an offence under section 9(d)."
-- A peaceful picket at a person's HOME is within the protection.
GIVEN `in contemplation or furtherance of a trade or work dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `merely to inform or peacefully persuade` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to obstruct the approach or exit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to lead to a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the picket is protected` IF
        `in contemplation or furtherance of a trade or work dispute`
    AND `merely to inform or peacefully persuade`
    AND (NOT `calculated to intimidate`)
    AND (NOT `calculated to obstruct the approach or exit`)
    AND (NOT `calculated to lead to a breach of the peace`)

GIVEN `in contemplation or furtherance of a trade or work dispute` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `merely to inform or peacefully persuade` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to obstruct the approach or exit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `calculated to lead to a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the picket is a deemed s 9(d) offence` IF
        `in contemplation or furtherance of a trade or work dispute`
    AND (`calculated to intimidate` OR `calculated to obstruct the approach or exit` OR `calculated to lead to a breach of the peace`)

§§ `11 -- dangerous breach of contract`

-- s 11: "Every person who wilfully and maliciously breaks a contract of service or of hiring, or a platform work agreement ...
-- knowing or having reason to believe that the probable consequences of his doing so, either alone or in combination with others,
-- will be to endanger human life or cause serious bodily injury, or to expose valuable property ... to destruction or serious
-- injury". s 2: "maliciously" means "the doing of a wrongful act intentionally without just cause or excuse".
GIVEN `wilfully breaks a contract of service, hiring or platform work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `without just cause or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knows or has reason to believe the probable consequence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the consequence is danger to life, serious injury or serious damage to valuable property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the breach of contract is an offence` IF
        `wilfully breaks a contract of service, hiring or platform work`
    AND `without just cause or excuse`
    AND `knows or has reason to believe the probable consequence`
    AND `the consequence is danger to life, serious injury or serious damage to valuable property`

§§ `12 to 14 -- prosecution`

-- s 12: "Every offence against the provisions of this Act shall be arrestable and non-bailable".
-- s 13: once a person is charged under s 5, 6 or 7, "no further proceedings ... shall be taken against him without the consent of
-- the Public Prosecutor", except remand and custody, and the section "shall not apply to proceedings instituted by or on behalf of
-- the Public Prosecutor ab initio".
-- s 14: offences under s 5, 6 or 7 "may be placed before the General Division of the High Court for trial"; every offence may be
-- prosecuted in a District Court or Magistrate's Court.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is under s 5, 6 or 7` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal industrial action` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal lockout` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `instigating an illegal industrial action or lockout` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `inciting a person bound by an award to industrial action` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `funding an illegal industrial action or lockout` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is arrestable and non-bailable` IF TRUE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `instituted by the Public Prosecutor from the start` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further proceedings need the Public Prosecutor's consent` IF
    `the offence is under s 5, 6 or 7` `the offence` AND (NOT `instituted by the Public Prosecutor from the start`)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be tried in the High Court` IF
    `the offence is under s 5, 6 or 7` `the offence`

§§ `15 -- conspiracy`

-- s 15(1): an agreement or combination by 2 or more persons to do an act "in contemplation or furtherance of a trade dispute between
-- employers and employees, or a work dispute between platform operators and platform workers, shall not be punishable as a
-- conspiracy if such act committed by one person would not be punishable as a crime". (5): a crime is an offence for which the
-- offender is liable "to be imprisoned either absolutely or at the discretion of the court".
-- (2): an act done under such an agreement "in contemplation or furtherance of a trade dispute or work dispute" is "not actionable
-- unless the act, if done without any such agreement or combination, would be actionable".
-- (3) a conspiracy punished by any written law; (4) riot, unlawful assembly, breach of the peace, offences against the State or the
-- President; (4A) contempt of court and offences under s 39 or 40 of the Maintenance of Racial Harmony Act 2025, s 17E or 17F of
-- the Maintenance of Religious Harmony Act 1990, or s 267C or 505 of the Penal Code 1871 -- all outside the shield.
-- (1) names only disputes "between employers and employees" or "between platform operators and platform workers"; (2) names any
-- "trade dispute or work dispute", which s 2 extends to disputes among employees, among employers, and among platform workers or
-- operators.
GIVEN `the parties` IS A Parties
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dispute is across the employment line` IF
    CONSIDER `the parties`
    WHEN `employers and employees` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `platform operators and platform workers` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the parties` IS A Parties,
      `connected with employment or its terms` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act alone would be imprisonable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `falls within a saving in s 15(3), (4) or (4A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(1) shields the combination from criminal conspiracy` IF
        `it is a trade dispute or work dispute` `the parties` `connected with employment or its terms`
    AND `the dispute is across the employment line` `the parties`
    AND (NOT `the act alone would be imprisonable`)
    AND (NOT `falls within a saving in s 15(3), (4) or (4A)`)

GIVEN `the parties` IS A Parties,
      `connected with employment or its terms` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the act alone would be actionable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(2) shields the combined act from civil action` IF
        `it is a trade dispute or work dispute` `the parties` `connected with employment or its terms`
    AND (NOT `the act alone would be actionable`)
